From: Patrick Quinn <patrick@jquinn.com>
Date: 2026-06-24
Subject: [PATCH] librem5: mark usdhc2 (BRCM WiFi) as non-removable

The Librem 5's usdhc2 hosts a soldered BRCM43752 SDIO WiFi/BT chip
(or RS9116 on r1 variants), NOT a removable microSD card. The upstream
Purism DTSI declares `cd-gpios = <&gpio2 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;` for
this slot but does NOT mark it `non-removable`. The MMC core then
polls the CD GPIO at probe time; on this hardware GPIO2:12 reads
"card absent" before the WiFi chip's power-on sequence completes,
so the SDIO probe skips the slot and the chip is never enumerated:

    mmc1: error -110 whilst initialising SDIO card

After boot the chip is fully powered (3V3_WIFI regulator enabled,
wlan-hks rfkill unblocked) but no driver ever sees it because the
SDIO bus is empty. NetworkManager reports `WIFI-HW: missing`, no
wlan0 interface exists.

`non-removable;` tells the MMC core that this slot has a soldered
device — skip CD polling, always assume the card is present, run
the SDIO probe unconditionally. This is the same fix mainline uses
for every other phone/board with soldered brcmfmac/rsi WiFi.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick@jquinn.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-librem5.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-librem5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-librem5.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-librem5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-librem5.dtsi
@@ -1812,6 +1812,7 @@
 	cd-gpios = <&gpio2 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	disable-wp;
 	cap-sdio-irq;
+	non-removable;
 	cap-power-off-card;
 	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	wakeup-source;
